## Settings

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SIDECUT_SKILL_LOG` | on | Set to `0` to turn off the local usage log described under Privacy |

In Codex, the usage log is a plugin hook, and Codex runs plugin hooks only after you trust them. Codex asks again whenever a hook changes.

## Privacy

The plugin keeps a local usage log unless you set `SIDECUT_SKILL_LOG=0`, and never when `DO_NOT_TRACK=1` is set or it runs in CI. Each time one of its skills runs in Claude Code, Codex or Antigravity, it adds one line to `~/.sidecut/skill-log.jsonl` with the fields `time`, `plugin`, `skill` and `host`. Nothing is sent anywhere.

